  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi There,\n\nI've recently made a console app (which also uses OpenVR overlay) to keep an eye on who's in & joined an instance. However, due to crashers/stealers still being a thing at the moment, I'd like to see user ids provided in the output logs next to the display/in-game names. The reason for suggesting this is because I do not wish to hit the VRChat API every few seconds just for getting userids. There's also some names which might not work with the API, such as names containing unicode characters.\n\nMy application reads the output log in real-time and gathers/logs every user I encounter and displays them in a console window. However the search function on the website is dodgy when it comes to unicode names. If the output logs contained a userid for every user encountered, it'll make reporting them a lot easier and with much greater accuracy so we don't report the wrong person.\n\nI've been streaming with my application for weeks now and it seems to have either been a really good repellent already or I'm just not running into them as much (or at all). I can provide clips of it if you wish to understand more about it. This application I've made before you ask, is not ready for public use as there's still some work needed to be done on it.\n\nUnless I'm allowed to hit the API every few seconds, I think it'll be best to provide the userids in the output logs.\nRegards, CM1",
